1
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:54,280
It's cold and delicious.

2
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:01,100
Someone's coming!

3
00:02:03,419 --> 00:02:08,560
I'm so bored. Isn't there anything fun to do?

4
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:11,200
There!

5
00:02:12,084 --> 00:02:13,580
Ah, this is so boring.

6
00:02:14,875 --> 00:02:16,300
What's with that kid?

7
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:20,860
Wandering around deep in the sacred woods... He must have way too much time on his hands.

8
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,220
Grandpa...

9
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,320
I know!

10
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:38,900
Grandpa! It's terrible, terrible!

11
00:02:39,404 --> 00:02:41,140
W-What's the matter, Mokku?

12
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:44,220
A-A-A-A-A-A monster appeared!

13
00:02:44,765 --> 00:02:48,480
Wh-What? A monster? Th-That's terrible!

14
00:02:50,614 --> 00:02:52,180
Holy Mother!

15
00:02:56,659 --> 00:02:59,480
Mother Mary, please save us!

16
00:03:07,550 --> 00:03:08,600
Where was it?

17
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:12,520
Deep in the heart of the forest!

18
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,160
In the forest?

19
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:17,160
In the forest?

20
00:03:18,590 --> 00:03:21,480
Yeah, there was a monster in the forest! A monster!

21
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:28,160
Lying to me again. I go into that forest all the time to gather materials for work.

22
00:03:28,439 --> 00:03:32,080
I know every single corner of it. There aren't any monsters there!

23
00:03:32,899 --> 00:03:34,040
Aw, you caught me.

24
00:03:35,110 --> 00:03:39,560
You little rascal. It's no good if you keep telling so many lies.

25
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:42,220
Come on, you're in the way of my work. Go play outside.

26
00:03:42,725 --> 00:03:45,860
Aw, please play with me! Just for a little bit!

27
00:03:46,835 --> 00:03:50,160
No, no, that won't do. Grandpa is busy.

28
00:03:50,265 --> 00:03:52,220
Hey there, old man. Looking healthy as ever.

29
00:03:52,655 --> 00:03:54,960
Why, hello, Mayor of Pieto.

30
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:57,860
Hm? What is that...?

31
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:02,340
Let me have a look.

32
00:04:02,794 --> 00:04:12,320
Oh, this is a magnificent statue of Mary. Old man, won't you part with this and sell it to me? / Heavens, no! I couldn't possibly give this to anyone. This is, well...

33
00:04:12,321 --> 00:04:14,380
Come now, I'll pay whatever you ask.

34
00:04:14,925 --> 00:04:18,579
This is something precious that money simply cannot buy.

35
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:20,920
I see. Well, that's a shame.

36
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:25,260
Grandpa really treasures that, doesn't he?

37
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:35,320
Isn't there anything fun to do?

38
00:04:36,770 --> 00:04:38,000
Coming! Who could that be?

39
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:49,220
The moon shines high over the sea, the wind is still, the waves are calm.

40
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:55,540
Tonight, my friends, the boat is waiting.

41
00:04:55,880 --> 00:05:02,740
Santa Lucia, Santa Lucia.

42
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:09,960
Come, my friends, let us look upon the sea.

43
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:17,860
Santa Lucia! Santa Lucia!

44
00:05:17,940 --> 00:05:20,420
He's certainly in shape from his time in the fire brigade.

45
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:25,520
Though if the fire chief is taking it so easy, it'd be bad news if a fire broke out.

46
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:31,480
I know! This'll be fun! I'll do it!

47
00:05:41,125 --> 00:05:42,125
All right, here goes!

48
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:44,160
One, two, three!

49
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:45,940
Fire!

50
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:47,760
Fire!

51
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:49,820
It's a fire!

52
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:52,260
Fire!

53
00:05:52,710 --> 00:05:53,710
Fire!

54
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,420
Where's the fire? Where? Where?

55
00:05:56,539 --> 00:05:57,539
Over there! Over there! Over there!

56
00:05:57,735 --> 00:05:58,800
Wh-What? What?

57
00:05:58,930 --> 00:05:59,930
Over there! Over there! Over there!

58
00:06:00,810 --> 00:06:03,060
That's toward the Mayor's house!

59
00:06:04,190 --> 00:06:05,190
The Mayor?

60
00:06:06,735 --> 00:06:08,380
Like I care about that!

61
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,820
Fire!

62
00:06:11,935 --> 00:06:13,360
Fire!

63
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:14,380
Fire!

64
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,060
Where's the fire?

65
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:17,780
Is it at the blacksmith's?

66
00:06:17,944 --> 00:06:20,640
No, toward the Mayor's house. What?!

67
00:06:20,641 --> 00:06:23,060
Hey! What about my food?!

68
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:26,240
There's no time for that! The Mayor's house is on fire!

69
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,740
Hooray! Give me my food already!

70
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:30,100
Okay!

71
00:06:31,555 --> 00:06:35,580
Fire!

72
00:06:35,835 --> 00:06:37,020
Fire!

73
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:38,380
Fire!

74
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:40,580
It's terrible!

75
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:41,720
Fire!

76
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,100
Where? Where is the fire?

77
00:06:53,670 --> 00:06:56,600
Kind ladies and gentlemen...

78
00:06:57,780 --> 00:06:58,780
Thank you very much.

79
00:06:59,165 --> 00:07:03,120
I'm poor myself, but some people have it even worse.

80
00:07:03,295 --> 00:07:06,120
May God bless your kind heart.

81
00:07:06,230 --> 00:07:07,980
Fire! There's a fire over there!

82
00:07:08,550 --> 00:07:10,000
What? A fire?

83
00:07:11,910 --> 00:07:13,600
Give me back my money!

84
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:15,360
Help!

85
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:17,640
Help!

86
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:19,020
Give it back!

87
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:24,140
Easy, easy...

88
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:34,900
Fire! Fire!

89
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:42,540
...C-C-Captain! There's a f-fire, sir!

90
00:07:42,665 --> 00:07:46,300
Fool! Don't panic! Putting out fires is our job!

91
00:07:46,625 --> 00:07:48,280
What's the point of jumping at every little thing?

92
00:07:49,670 --> 00:07:52,400
Just when I was happily singing my song...

93
00:07:53,170 --> 00:07:54,780
Where is this insolent fire?

94
00:07:55,240 --> 00:08:00,040
W-W-Well, it's at the m-m-mayor's house, sir... Wh-What?!

95
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:07,520
Why didn't you say that first?!

96
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
I'm terribly sorry!

97
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:13,040
Hurry up and move out already!

98
00:08:14,094 --> 00:08:16,840
(Laughter)

99
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:38,900
Roberto, where is the fire?

100
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:43,500
Ma'am, the fire is at the mayor's residence!

101
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:45,980
Make sure you do a thorough job, now.

102
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:57,080
All right!

103
00:08:57,380 --> 00:08:59,600
What on earth is all this ruckus?!

104
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:03,860
Dumping all this water when the sun is blazing hot, you clumsy fools!

105
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:07,600
Who was it?! Who's the one that said my house was on fire?!

106
00:09:07,601 --> 00:09:09,960
Ah... ah-choo!

107
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:16,700
Thanks to you, I got soaked with water... Ah-choo! Now I've caught a cold!

108
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:18,000
Ah-choo!

109
00:09:18,540 --> 00:09:22,080
Who lied?! Who started this?!

110
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:30,420
It's him! That little shrimp!

111
00:09:33,539 --> 00:09:35,180
He's the one who said it first!

112
00:09:36,565 --> 00:09:38,720
(Boy) No! It wasn't me!

113
00:09:38,865 --> 00:09:42,940
(Man) Ah, right, I remember now! Running around screaming "Fire! Fire!" It was definitely him!

114
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,420
(Girl) No, you're wrong!

115
00:09:44,809 --> 00:09:49,840
(Man) No, it was! I saw it with my own eyes, and I remember that face! Right?

116
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:56,120
(Man) Ah, no, wait, my mistake. I heard it with my own ears, and I remember the voice! Right? (Man) Yeah, what a wretched brat. With a face like a demon!

117
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:57,920
(Man) That's right! Wring his neck!

118
00:09:58,155 --> 00:09:59,960
(Man) How's that?! Still denying it, you little bastard?!

119
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:01,760
(Girl) Ah... (Man) You little bastard!

120
00:10:01,850 --> 00:10:02,850
(Man) Get him!

121
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:05,540
(Screams)

122
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:12,480
Grandpa, help me!

123
00:10:14,455 --> 00:10:19,300
Hey, wait! Mr. Mayor, please! I beg you, forgive him!

124
00:10:20,254 --> 00:10:23,580
A troublemaker like that needs to be taught a proper lesson.

125
00:10:23,795 --> 00:10:27,960
But if you do any more, he's going to die!

126
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:31,600
"He"? So then, old man... I am terribly sorry.

127
00:10:33,490 --> 00:10:35,320
Oh, it's the old man.

128
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,400
Good timing!

129
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:41,880
Hey, everyone, stop it. Let him off now.

130
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:43,620
Thank you.

131
00:10:43,815 --> 00:10:46,780
By the way, old man, how about hearing me out?

132
00:10:48,709 --> 00:10:50,260
That was horrible, just horrible!

133
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:53,640
They all ganged up on me, hitting and kicking me!

134
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,560
What are you going to do about this?!

135
00:10:57,370 --> 00:11:00,700
This boy understands nothing.

136
00:11:01,430 --> 00:11:06,680
My legs are broken so I can't walk! My arms are broken so I can't hold anything!

137
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:08,220
Fix me right away!

138
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:15,460
Grandpa, I understand now. I won't lie or trick people anymore, so please fix me, Grandpa!

139
00:11:16,205 --> 00:11:20,380
It must be my fault. Mine, for creating Mokku.

140
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:22,920
Hurry up and fix me!

141
00:11:25,369 --> 00:11:28,040
I swear I'll never lie again!

142
00:11:29,315 --> 00:11:34,180
No, no, he still doesn't understand. He's just paying lip service because he wants to be put back together.

143
00:11:34,615 --> 00:11:39,440
I have to harden my heart until he truly understands, for his own sake.

144
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:45,680
Grandpa! Leaving me like this is just too cruel!

145
00:11:46,539 --> 00:11:48,040
Let me see, let me see!

146
00:11:48,915 --> 00:11:54,600
Ah, look at that. Poor Mokku, he's in such a pitiful mess, I wonder why.

147
00:11:54,900 --> 00:11:56,400
You've come at just the right time.

148
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,940
Because we're friends... I wonder why.

149
00:11:59,470 --> 00:12:01,900
Hey, put that one over there on for me.

150
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:04,440
Brother, what should we do?

151
00:12:04,685 --> 00:12:06,260
Just do what he says.

152
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:12,380
Ah, Mokku.

153
00:12:17,289 --> 00:12:18,289
Wait, Mokku!

154
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:33,940
(Grandpa laughing)

155
00:12:36,220 --> 00:12:36,700
(Laughter)

156
00:12:36,701 --> 00:12:39,160
What was with that shocked look on Grandpa's face?

157
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:41,320
Ah, that's hilarious!

158
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:42,980
(Laughter)

159
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:43,740
(Gasping)

160
00:12:43,741 --> 00:12:44,940
I'm so thirsty.

161
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:47,200
(Gasping)

162
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:48,400
(Gasping)

163
00:12:48,401 --> 00:12:48,780
(Gasping)

164
00:12:48,781 --> 00:12:49,320
(Gasping)

165
00:12:49,321 --> 00:12:49,680
(Gasping)

166
00:12:49,681 --> 00:12:49,900
(Gasping)

167
00:12:49,901 --> 00:12:50,901
(Gasping)

168
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:57,341
And here is the reasoning. Since it says "read this,"

169
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:13,680
Since it says "read this," while creating confusion, if the letters become clearly visible here, enter those letters and the character name, so whether it is this character's name or not.

170
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:15,460
Yes.

171
00:13:16,799 --> 00:13:18,540
Ah, this is my Japanese...

172
00:13:19,909 --> 00:13:21,720
You're being a good boy, aren't you, Mokku?

173
00:13:22,245 --> 00:13:25,840
Yeah, of course. Everyone's always praising me for being good.

174
00:13:27,354 --> 00:13:30,220
You haven't been lying or deceiving people, have you?

175
00:13:30,795 --> 00:13:34,180
No way. My teacher says I'm a really good boy.

176
00:13:35,030 --> 00:13:36,500
Huh? What's happening to my nose?

177
00:13:36,975 --> 00:13:39,800
You haven't done anything to make Grandfather sad, have you?

178
00:13:40,795 --> 00:13:44,060
Definitely not. Grandpa is always so happy...

179
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:47,780
Mokku, it is no use trying to deceive me.

180
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:53,440
Whenever you lie in front of me, your nose will grow as punishment.

181
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:55,100
T-That's not fair!

182
00:13:56,170 --> 00:14:00,120
You must not cause trouble for people who are trying to help each other.

183
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:03,340
My nose... it's so heavy!

184
00:14:03,685 --> 00:14:05,700
Mokku, are you listening to me?

185
00:14:06,645 --> 00:14:10,600
If you can only think of yourself, you will never become a real human.

186
00:14:10,735 --> 00:14:13,820
I'm listening! But my nose is so heavy, I can't concentrate!

187
00:14:14,549 --> 00:14:18,420
In other words, you must never lie or deceive others.

188
00:14:19,060 --> 00:14:21,000
I understand. I won't do it again.

189
00:14:22,340 --> 00:14:24,360
It seems those words are not a lie.

190
00:14:25,175 --> 00:14:28,340
Very well. Just this once, I will return it to normal.

191
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:58,080
(Good night)

192
00:15:02,580 --> 00:15:05,820
Thank goodness! Thank you so much, Fairy!

193
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,280
Huh?

194
00:15:07,435 --> 00:15:09,820
Be a good boy, Mokku.

195
00:15:10,895 --> 00:15:12,760
Try your very best, Mokku.

196
00:15:14,349 --> 00:15:17,160
And become a real human as soon as you can.

197
00:15:19,379 --> 00:15:23,020
Yes, I understand. I won't ever tell a lie again.

198
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,200
(Boys' chatter)

199
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:33,300
(Boys' chatter)

200
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:36,440
(Boys' chatter)

201
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:38,020
(Boys' chatter)

202
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:42,000
That looks like fun! Hey, let me play too!

203
00:15:43,555 --> 00:15:45,280
Come on, let me try!

204
00:15:45,435 --> 00:15:47,220
No way. We're not letting Mokku play with us.

205
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:48,460
Why not?

206
00:15:48,880 --> 00:15:49,880
Because you're a liar.

207
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:50,660
What?

208
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:54,080
My mom told me not to play with liars.

209
00:15:54,485 --> 00:15:56,860
Yeah. Come on, everyone, let's go!

210
00:15:57,840 --> 00:15:58,840
Hey!

211
00:15:58,940 --> 00:15:59,080
Hey!

212
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,500
Hey!

213
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:03,560
Hey!

214
00:16:03,709 --> 00:16:07,780
Why? Even after I promised not to lie anymore...

215
00:16:19,219 --> 00:16:20,980
Boss, it's ready.

216
00:16:25,219 --> 00:16:28,380
Ready? I tied you up tight with multiple ropes.

217
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:29,560
Yes.

218
00:16:29,770 --> 00:16:31,300
Then put the lock on.

219
00:16:32,140 --> 00:16:32,440
Yes, sir.

220
00:16:32,739 --> 00:16:34,660
One, two, three!

221
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,240
Amazing!

222
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:40,040
We're not done yet!

223
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:43,700
This time, he's wrapped up from head to toe!

224
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:44,900
All right!

225
00:16:49,259 --> 00:16:50,760
Shall we put the hood over him this time?

226
00:16:51,190 --> 00:16:52,190
No hood this time!

227
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:53,740
Take a look at this!

228
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,200
Incredible!

229
00:16:57,340 --> 00:16:58,800
I wonder why?

230
00:16:59,805 --> 00:17:01,920
Are you feeling a little better?

231
00:17:02,515 --> 00:17:05,300
Thank you. Grandfather, you're amazing.

232
00:17:06,009 --> 00:17:09,500
Look, four thieves and three nasties. Why is that?

233
00:17:11,140 --> 00:17:13,819
But bro, if this keeps up, he's gonna...

234
00:17:13,980 --> 00:17:16,819
Idiot, leave him alone. The real show is just starting.

235
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:18,319
Um... why is that?

236
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:26,040
You're pretty incredible yourself. You turned the whole town upside down with that little tongue of yours. I was amazed watching it!

237
00:17:30,174 --> 00:17:33,080
If it's a fun game, will you teach me?

238
00:17:33,204 --> 00:17:37,600
It's super fun even on your own! Yeah, teach me!

239
00:17:49,489 --> 00:17:51,580
All right, come on.

240
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:53,640
Okay.

241
00:17:57,880 --> 00:18:02,240
This is it. Huh? This is Butterfly's house.

242
00:18:02,869 --> 00:18:04,720
What are we going to do at Butterfly's house?

243
00:18:05,610 --> 00:18:07,920
We're gonna steal the gold leaf from this house!

244
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,160
Steal?

245
00:18:09,919 --> 00:18:14,500
Hehehehe. Just figuring that out now, you runt?

246
00:18:16,689 --> 00:18:18,500
Hehehehehe.

247
00:18:18,779 --> 00:18:20,460
Shut up and do what you're told!

248
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,120
*(crying)*

249
00:18:34,569 --> 00:18:36,560
I...

250
00:18:37,639 --> 00:18:38,960
Are you back?

251
00:18:51,634 --> 00:18:53,500
All right, this is it!

252
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:59,300
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8... Wow, so bright!

253
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:02,440
It was so emotional!

254
00:19:16,759 --> 00:19:18,840
Hey, did something happen to you too?

255
00:19:31,340 --> 00:19:33,221
Good night. What are you doing?

256
00:19:33,319 --> 00:19:34,720
Are you throwing that away?

257
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:36,400
What are you doing?

258
00:19:37,639 --> 00:19:39,200
Toma, you're talking too loud. Keep it down.

259
00:19:39,745 --> 00:19:42,320
Help me carry this money chest.

260
00:19:42,739 --> 00:19:45,400
You'll be able to buy as many of those wooden puppets as you want.

261
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:46,720
Just do it.

262
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:50,200
What the...?!

263
00:19:50,300 --> 00:19:51,300
Who's there?!

264
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:56,520
Thief!

265
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:58,000
Damn it!

266
00:20:00,110 --> 00:20:01,110
Thief!

267
00:20:01,365 --> 00:20:02,365
Stop!

268
00:20:12,829 --> 00:20:13,880
You little brat!

269
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:15,480
This is outrageous!

270
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:16,660
This is outrageous!

271
00:20:17,704 --> 00:20:20,580
What the... Wait, please!

272
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:25,080
Please, just don't break him! I'm begging you!

273
00:20:25,195 --> 00:20:26,195
Grandpa...

274
00:20:28,164 --> 00:20:32,180
Mayor, I just can't believe he's the kind of boy who would steal.

275
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:34,400
That's just a parent's blind bias.

276
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:38,700
I actually caught him red-handed! He completely emptied out my safe!

277
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:40,120
The mayor is right.

278
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:47,460
Last time, I let it slide in exchange for that statue of Mary I wanted, but this time I won't let him off!

279
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:49,160
A statue of Mary?

280
00:20:52,269 --> 00:20:58,100
Today, Grandpa, just to save me, you gave up that statue of Mary you loved so much...

281
00:20:58,245 --> 00:21:00,340
It is all right, Mokku.

282
00:21:00,659 --> 00:21:04,660
Grandpa, why are you so good to a bad boy like me?

283
00:21:06,919 --> 00:21:10,580
I'm just a liar who causes nothing but trouble.

284
00:21:10,834 --> 00:21:17,580
It is all right, Mokku. The holy Mother Mary atoned for your sins.

285
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:23,580
Grandpa...

286
00:21:25,529 --> 00:21:27,400
Who cares?! Smash it to pieces!

287
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:44,880
Wait a minute!

288
00:21:46,479 --> 00:21:50,360
Mayor! This guy had all the stolen gold bars and jewels!

289
00:21:50,794 --> 00:21:52,380
What!?

290
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:55,940
Mokku was only tricked and used. This guy is the one to blame!

291
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:59,860
I see... So that's how it was... You bastard!

292
00:22:01,195 --> 00:22:05,720
Mokku! We blew it because you were gawking at that stupid statue of Mary!

293
00:22:06,549 --> 00:22:08,760
The statue of Mary...

294
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:14,900
That statue of Mary... Mokku did that...

295
00:22:16,980 --> 00:22:23,560
I'm sorry, Mokku. For doubting you. I will return the statue of Mary to your grandpa.

296
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:25,960
Grandpa!

297
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:40,000
(sobbing)

298
00:22:58,079 --> 00:22:59,079
Hello there.

299
00:22:59,519 --> 00:23:02,060
Hello. Um, who are you?

300
00:23:02,849 --> 00:23:03,860
M-Me?

301
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:09,620
Well, um... I'd hate to tell such a pretty girl that I'm a puppet.

302
00:23:10,094 --> 00:23:11,740
I'm Mokku from the castle.

303
00:23:12,449 --> 00:23:15,280
Wow, from the castle? Then are you a prince?

304
00:23:15,520 --> 00:23:16,620
Well, something like that.

305
00:23:17,829 --> 00:23:19,960
Prince Mokku of the castle.

306
00:23:20,320 --> 00:23:21,320
(Laughter)

307
00:23:33,259 --> 00:23:38,280
While teasing Mokku, mischievous Cole slips and falls into the river.

308
00:23:39,884 --> 00:23:42,500
And despite Mokku's efforts to save him, he dies.

309
00:23:43,540 --> 00:23:48,740
Mokku tries to gently comfort Cole's mother, who is overwhelmed with grief after losing her only son...

310
00:23:49,264 --> 00:23:56,920
Yet she refuses to listen to him, coldly pushing Mokku away as he tries to take Cole's place.

311
00:23:57,689 --> 00:24:00,700
Don't miss next week's Kashi no Ki Mokku!

